From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: isilweo <isilweo@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:50:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: thinksmart: mark headphone detect normally open

The ThinkSmart View has no headphone jack. Its codec interprets the
unconnected HPHL detect line as a plugged-in jack with the default
normally closed setting.

Describe the line as normally open so the codec reports no plug.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/5660e8900869c02ce4b858ac97fdac0cf2bb755f
Base-commit: 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
index 658e8f71a573..470c39ba5ee6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
@@ -414,6 +414,12 @@ &wcd_codec {
 	vdd-micbias-supply = <&vph_pwr>;
 
 	qcom,micbias1-ext-cap;
+	/*
+	 * There is no headphone jack and the HPHL detect line is not
+	 * connected. Treat it as a normally open jack, so that the open line
+	 * reads as nothing plugged in.
+	 */
+	qcom,hphl-jack-type-normally-open;
 
 	status = "okay";
 };
